test_command=sh tests/sluglimit_test.sh && sh tests/antz-flow_test.sh && sh tests/orchestrator-sessionguards_test.sh && sh tests/skills-activation-prompts_test.sh && sh tests/renderinject_test.sh
id=sluglimit-01 result=green reason=unit test "sluglimit-01: the step 1 slug-derivation bullet states the derived slug is at most 40 characters -- the flow script's mechanical state=bad_slug length limit, matched to its -le value -- in place of the undefined short, so a derived slug passes the gate rather than relying on it as a catch" (tests/sluglimit_test.sh) passes -- the bullet now reads "derive a kebab-case slug of at most 40 characters -- the flow script's mechanical `state=bad_slug` length limit, so a derived slug passes that gate rather than relying on it as a catch -- from the raw request, ...": the undefined "short" is gone from the bullet (refuse check), kebab-case survives, the stated number is cross-checked against the flow script's own `-le` value on the bad_slug gate line (so a future script-side limit change bites the bullet), and the invariant holds: scripts/orchestration/antz-flow.sh is byte-unchanged vs HEAD (git diff --quiet asserted in the test)
id=sluglimit-02 result=green reason=unit test "sluglimit-02: the bullet keeps the collision rules' pinned meaning -- suffix only on continuation with the spdd/changes/, spdd/archive/ and antz/* collision checks, and the ask-the-user stop on a semantically unclear continuation -- while the only prompt line changed vs HEAD is the derivation bullet itself" (tests/sluglimit_test.sh) passes -- the bullet's collision tail from "from the raw request," onward is byte-identical to HEAD's, with explicit pins of the three collision checks (`spdd/changes/`, `spdd/archive/`, `git branch --list 'antz/*'`), the suffix-only-on-continuation clause, and the ask-the-user stop on a semantically unclear continuation (never a bare "-2" without semantic continuation -- the flow-07 waiting-user slug-ambiguity report pin still reads unchanged in the prompt); the diff of agents/prompts/orchestrator.prompt vs HEAD is exactly one removed and one added line, and those are verbatim HEAD's and the working derivation bullets (only-the-bullet-changed invariant), while the structural spot checks stay green: numbered steps end at 6, the fence count and table rows equal HEAD's, the dedup guard keeps "exactly two exceptions, both step 4"; surrounding pins all pass unmodified (tests/antz-flow_test.sh 52 passed, orchestrator-sessionguards/skills-activation-prompts/renderinject orchestrator-prose gates self-retired with their established mechanism -- loud notes printed by the prompts and sessionguards suites, renderinject's gate retiring via its documented degenerate-base path -- no test edits required; full regression: all 26 tests/*_test.sh suites green, 0 failed)
